<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfred Dent</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1844–1927</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfred Dent was a British merchant who, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-von-overbeck">Baron von Overbeck</a>, obtained concessions in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a> from the sultans of Brunei and Sulu in 1877 and 1878. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-north-borneo-company">British North Borneo Company</a>, which received a royal charter in 1881 and governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">North Borneo</a> until 1946.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfred-dent.jpg" alt="Alfred Dent" width="320" height="473" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AlfredDent.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
